TITLE: Final Report

LangChain implements its callback system through a structured architecture located in `langchain_core.callbacks`. The implementation relies on two primary components:

*   **`BaseCallbackHandler`** (defined in `libs/core/langchain_core/callbacks/base.py`): This class serves as the base interface for listening to lifecycle events within LangChain, such as the start or end of LLM calls, chain executions, or tool usage.
*   **`CallbackManager`** (defined in `libs/core/langchain_core/callbacks/manager.py`): This acts as the orchestrator. It manages the registration of callback handlers and triggers the appropriate methods on those handlers during the execution lifecycle of LangChain components.

By registering handlers with a `CallbackManager`, users can hook into various events throughout the execution flow to implement logging, tracing, or custom logic.

